efense: Najdorf Variation, Adams Attack","as":"w","accuracy":{"w":95.4,"b":86.9},"counts":{"w":{"best":20,"brilliant":1,"great":4},"b":{"best":23,"mistake":2,"blunder":1}},"moment":{"name":"20.Rxd6","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","fen":"4r2r/1pkb1p2/p1nR1Pp1/6Pp/4p3/1NP1B2P/P1P2KB1/7R b - - 0 20","from":"d1","to":"d6"},"finalFen":"2k5/3R1p2/pNp2Pp1/6Pp/4rB1K/2r5/P7/8 b - - 19 39"},"white":"Ivan Saric","black":"MarcAndria Maurizzi","labels":["book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","book","best","best","best","best","best","forced","best","best","best","best","excellent","best","best","best","best","best","best","inaccuracy","best","best","excellent","mistake","brilliant","best","great","best","best","best","good","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","best","great","best","best","best","good","best","excellent","best","best","best","best","mistake","excellent","inaccuracy","great","forced","great","blunder","best","best","best"],"moments":[{"ply":38,"name":"19…Bd6","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"19…Bd6 is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 39% to 19%.","points":["White answers 20.Rxd6, which takes the bishop on d6.","Better was 19…h4 (+1.26): gains space: the pawn on h4 cramps White's pieces behind it."],"better":"19…h4 prepares …Bf5 and …Kc8 and gains space on the kingside. After 20.Rhe1 Bf5 21.Bf4+ Kc8 22.Rd5 Rd8 23.Bxe4 Bxh3 24.Rd3 Rxd3 25.cxd3 Kd7, the rooks are traded (+1.26)."},{"ply":39,"name":"20.Rxd6","cls":"brilliant","color":"w","headline":"20.Rxd6!! A real sacrifice: White gives up material and the engine still rates it best.","points":["Puts the rook on d6 where it can be taken.","Black can take, but after 20…Kxd6 21.Bf4+ Re5 22.Rd1+ the engine rates it +3.57.","Takes the bishop on d6.","20.Rxd6 takes the bishop on d6.","Black answers 20…Kxd6, winning the exchange.","After 20…Kxd6 21.Bf4+ Re5 22.Rd1+ Kc7 23.Nc5, White is two pawns down (+3.57)."],"why":[{"title":"The idea","text":"20.Rxd6!! offers the rook on d6. Taking it gives White an attack worth more than the rook."},{"title":"What White gives up","text":"20.Rxd6 puts the rook on d6 where it can be taken by the king. That's a whole rook on offer."},{"title":"What it does instead","text":"It takes the bishop on d6. Black has no bishop left to guard the dark squares around the king (b6, b8, d8)."},{"title":"If Black takes the rook","text":"20…Kxd6 is met by 21.Bf4+. Then 22.Rd1+ gives check, and 23.Na5+ gives check. White is still two pawns down, but the attack is worth more: White is clearly better (+2.38). This is Black's best try."},{"title":"Without the sacrifice","text":"The best move without the sacrifice, 20.Nd2, is clearly weaker (+1.49 against +3.57). Black answers 20…Be5, attacking the c3 pawn, which is undefended. That would leave White a little better."}]},{"ply":41,"name":"21.Bf4+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"21.Bf4+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Gives check, so the reply is forced.","The next best move, 21.Nc5, would drop White's winning chances from 81% to 68% (+2.03).","21.Bf4+ gives check.","Black answers 21…Ne5.","After 21…Ne5 22.Rd1+ Kc6 23.Na5+ Kb6 24.Bxe5 e3+, White comes out a piece up (+3.55)."]},{"ply":57,"name":"29.Ne5","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"29.Ne5! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Attacks the f7 pawn, which is undefended.","Centralises the knight on e5, where it reaches the most squares.","The next best move, 29.Rc1, would drop White's winning chances from 73% to 50% (0.00).","29.Ne5 threatens Nxf7, winning a pawn.","It threatens Nxf7, winning a pawn, so Black has to spend the next move on it.","Black answers 29…Rxc3+, winning a pawn."]},{"ply":68,"name":"34…Rf8","cls":"mistake","color":"b","headline":"34…Rf8 is a mistake: Black's winning chances go from 26% to 11%.","points":["White answers 35.Rb1: the rook takes the open b-file.","Better was 34…Rxe5 (+2.88), which takes the knight on e5."],"better":"34…Rxe5 stops Nxf7. After 35.Bxe5 Rc4+ 36.Kh3 Rg4 37.Rd6 Rxg5 38.Rxc6+ Kd7, Black is two pawns down (+2.88)."},{"ply":71,"name":"36.Nb6+","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"36.Nb6+! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["The knight joins the attack: it now hits 2 squares around the Black king.","Check, and Black has only one legal reply.","The next best move, 36.Ne5, would drop White's winning chances from 93% to 73% (+2.73).","36.Nb6+ joins the attack on the king and gives check, leaving one reply.","Black answers 36…Kb7, attacking the knight on b6, which is undefended.","After 36…Kb7 37.Na4 Kc8 38.Nxc3 Rd8 39.Rxd8+ Kxd8 40.Ne4, the rooks are traded and White comes out the exchange plus a pawn up (+7.70)."]},{"ply":73,"name":"37.Na4","cls":"great","color":"w","headline":"37.Na4! The only good move here: every alternative is clearly worse.","points":["Attacks the rook on c3, which is undefended.","Moves the attacked knight to safety.","The next best move, 37.Rb1, would drop White's winning chances from 94% to 50% (0.00).","37.Na4 wins a rook, picking it up with 38.Nxc3, and threatens Rd7+, with mate in 2.","Sets up a sequence and wins a rook once the captures settle, picking it up with 38.Nxc3.","It threatens Rd7+, with mate in 2, so Black has to spend the next move on it."]},{"ply":74,"name":"37…Re4","cls":"blunder","color":"b","headline":"37…Re4 is a blunder: Black's winning chances go from 6% to 0%. It allows mate in 2.","points":["White answers 38.Rd7+: the rook forks the king and the pawn: both can't be saved at once.","Better was 37…Kc8 (+7.56)."],"better":"37…Kc8 stops the mate threat Rd7+. After 38.Nxc3 Rd8 39.Rxd8+ Kxd8 40.Ne4 Ke8, the rooks are traded and Black is the exchange plus a pawn down (+7.56)."}],"opening":{"name":"Sicilian Defense: Najdorf Variation, Adams Attack","eco":"B90","points":["Both sides followed opening theory up to 8…d5: 16 moves in all, 8 by White and 8 by Black.","Theory runs out after 8…d5: too few games between strong players reached this position to go further."]}}